{"content_hash": "f9d9bbeaee69d109", "version_id": 417, "article_id": 42, "level_code": "ja_n4", "lang": "ja", "level": 2, "level_label": "N4 初級", "title": "月面着陸を支えたソフト開発者、マーガレット・ハミルトンさんが90歳で死去", "title_zh": "让阿波罗11号成功登月的软件工程师玛格丽特·汉密尔顿去世，享年90岁", "has_translation": true, "topic": "science", "source": "guardian_science", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/oct/07/margaret-hamilton-moon-computer-software", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1520908695049-da13395b27a6?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MXx8bWFyZ2FyZXQlMjBoYW1pbHRvbnxlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkxNTk0Mzc2fDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Keith Luke on Unsplash", "author": "Keith Luke", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@lukephotography?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/red-house-beside-body-of-water-with-white-motor-boats-during-daytime-Ad2BXIYc_gc?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(116, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(154, 46%, 48%)", "label": "SCIENCE", "seed": "1c94d1b8ff91"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 152, "reading_minutes": 0.5, "lead": "アポロ11号の月面着陸を支えたソフトウェアを作ったマーガレット・ハミルトンさんが亡くなりました。90歳でした。MITが水曜日に発表しました。", "lead_zh": "为阿波罗11号登月提供关键软件的玛格丽特·汉密尔顿去世，享年90岁。麻省理工学院（MIT）于周三公布了这一消息。", "preview": "ハミルトンさんは、ソフトウェア技術者という言葉がまだなかった時代に、MITでプログラミングを学びました。彼女は敵の飛行機を見つけるソフトを作りました。その後、NASAのアポロ計画の飛行ソフトの開発に参加しました。彼女は最初のプログラマーで、最初の女性でした。", "preview_zh": "汉密尔顿在还没有“软件工程师”这个词的年代，就在MIT学习编程。她写过发现敌机的软件。后来，她参加了NASA阿波罗计划飞行软件的开发。她是第一位程序员，也是第一位女性。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 407, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/42/ja_n4.mp3", "duration": 32.25, "size_bytes": 197280, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 92, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@0a373f3/content/data/versions/417.json", "paragraphs": ["ハミルトンさんは、ソフトウェア技術者という言葉がまだなかった時代に、MITでプログラミングを学びました。彼女は敵の飛行機を見つけるソフトを作りました。その後、NASAのアポロ計画の飛行ソフトの開発に参加しました。彼女は最初のプログラマーで、最初の女性でした。", "1969年、アポロ11号が月に着陸する数分前、船内のコンピューターの警報が鳴りました。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["汉密尔顿在还没有“软件工程师”这个词的年代，就在MIT学习编程。她写过发现敌机的软件。后来，她参加了NASA阿波罗计划飞行软件的开发。她是第一位程序员，也是第一位女性。", "1969年，阿波罗11号登月前几分钟，飞船上的电脑警报响了，提示出现紧急情况。但任务没有中止。因为汉密尔顿和团队写的软件正好发挥了作用。"], "body": "ハミルトンさんは、ソフトウェア技術者という言葉がまだなかった時代に、MITでプログラミングを学びました。彼女は敵の飛行機を見つけるソフトを作りました。その後、NASAのアポロ計画の飛行ソフトの開発に参加しました。彼女は最初のプログラマーで、最初の女性でした。\n\n1969年、アポロ11号が月に着陸する数分前、船内のコンピューターの警報が鳴りました。", "body_zh": "汉密尔顿在还没有“软件工程师”这个词的年代，就在MIT学习编程。她写过发现敌机的软件。后来，她参加了NASA阿波罗计划飞行软件的开发。她是第一位程序员，也是第一位女性。\n\n1969年，阿波罗11号登月前几分钟，飞船上的电脑警报响了，提示出现紧急情况。但任务没有中止。因为汉密尔顿和团队写的软件正好发挥了作用。", "text": "ハミルトンさんは、ソフトウェア技術者という言葉がまだなかった時代に、MITでプログラミングを学びました。彼女は敵の飛行機を見つけるソフトを作りました。その後、NASAのアポロ計画の飛行ソフトの開発に参加しました。彼女は最初のプログラマーで、最初の女性でした。 1969年、アポロ11号が月に着陸する数分前、船内のコンピューターの警報が鳴りました。", "vocab": [{"word": "月面着陸", "pos": "noun", "zh": "月面着陆，登月", "note": "「月面」+「着陸」的组合词"}, {"word": "ソフトウェア", "pos": "noun", "zh": "软件", "note": "外来语，常简称为「ソフト」"}, {"word": "亡くなる", "pos": "verb", "zh": "去世", "note": "比「死ぬ」更礼貌的说法"}, {"word": "開発", "pos": "noun", "zh": "开发", "note": "常与「する」搭配：開発する"}, {"word": "警報", "pos": "noun", "zh": "警报", "note": "注意读音：けいほう"}, {"word": "緊急事態", "pos": "noun", "zh": "紧急情况", "note": "「緊急」+「事態」"}, {"word": "中止", "pos": "noun", "zh": "中止，取消", "note": "常与「になる」搭配：中止になる"}, {"word": "補う", "pos": "verb", "zh": "弥补，补偿", "note": "おぎなう，五段动词"}, {"word": "勲章", "pos": "noun", "zh": "勋章", "note": "大統領自由勲章 = 总统自由勋章"}, {"word": "先駆者", "pos": "noun", "zh": "先驱，开拓者", "note": "せんくしゃ，指走在前面的人"}], "title_original": "Margaret Hamilton, trailblazer whose software powered Apollo 11 moon landing, dies aged 90", "summary_original": "MIT computer scientist led development of software for moon mission and earned Presidential Medal of Freedom\nMargaret Hamilton, the computer pioneer whose software powered the first moon landing, has died, the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT)\nannounced\non Wednesday. She was 90.\nIn an era before titles such as software engineer and computer scientist became mainstream, Hamilton, who died on 30 September, learned to program under the tutelage of a renowned MIT meteorologist.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "Margaret Hamilton, trailblazer whose software powered Apollo 11 moon landing, dies aged 90\nMIT computer scientist led development of software for moon mission and earned Presidential Medal of Freedom\nMargaret Hamilton, the computer pioneer whose software powered the first moon landing, has died, the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT)\nannounced\non Wednesday. She was 90.\nIn an era before titles such as software engineer and computer scientist became mainstream, Hamilton, who died on 30 September, learned to program under the tutelage of a renowned MIT meteorologist.\nShe continued to perfect the craft in an MIT laboratory, writing software that could detect enemy aircraft. When the institute received a Nasa contract to develop the Apollo onboard flight software, she jumped at the opportunity.\n“I was attracted both by the sheer idea and the fact that it had never been done before. I was the first programmer to join and the first woman they hired,” she\ntold\nthe Guardian in 2019.\nIn 1969, minutes before the\nApollo 11\nspacecraft was set to make history by landing on the lunar surface, an onboard computer’s alarm rang, indicating an emergency.\nFaced with a decision of whether to abort the mission, the spacecraft continued on. The software was working just as Hamilton and her team intended.\n“It quickly became clear the software was not only informing everyone that there was a hardware-related problem but was compensating for it – restarting and re-establishing the highest priority tasks. The error detection and recovery mechanisms had come to the rescue,” Hamilton said.\nBarack Obama referenced the incident when he presented her with the Presidential Medal of Freedom in 2016.\n“Our astronauts didn’t have much time, but thankfully they had Margaret Hamilton,” he said.\nHamilton is survived by her daughter, a son-in-law, two grandsons and four great-grandchildren,\naccording\nto MIT.\nReflecting on the mission, in a 2009\ninterview\nwith MIT News, Hamilton said: “Looking back, we were the luckiest people in the world; there was no choice but to be pioneers; no time to be beginners.”\nExplore more on these topics\nSpace\nApollo 11\nThe moon\nComputing\nnews\nShare\nReuse this content", "fetched_at": "2026-10-10T01:06:14.236394", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "ハミルトン", "s": 0.125, "e": 0.7, "sm": 125, "em": 700, "cs": 0, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "さん", "s": 0.713, "e": 0.963, "sm": 712, "em": 962, "cs": 5, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "は", "s": 0.975, "e": 1.262, "sm": 975, "em": 1262, "cs": 7, "ce": 8, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "、", "s": 1.262, "e": 1.525, "sm": 1262, "em": 1525, "cs": 8, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "ソフトウェア", "s": 1.525, "e": 2.15, "sm": 1525, "em": 2150, "cs": 9, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "技術者", "s": 2.163, "e": 2.725, "sm": 2162, "em": 2725, "cs": 15, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "と", "s": 2.737, "e": 2.837, "sm": 2737, "em": 2837, "cs": 18, "ce": 19, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "いう", "s": 2.85, "e": 3.087, "sm": 2850, "em": 3087, "cs": 19, "ce": 21, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "言葉", "s": 3.1, "e": 3.462, "sm": 3100, "em": 3462, "cs": 21, "ce": 23, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "が", "s": 3.475, "e": 3.6, "sm": 3475, "em": 3600, "cs": 23, "ce": 24, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "まだ", "s": 3.612, "e": 3.887, "sm": 3612, "em": 3887, "cs": 24, "ce": 26, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "なかっ", "s": 3.9, "e": 4.237, "sm": 3900, "em": 4237, "cs": 26, "ce": 29, "si": 0}, {"i": 12, "w": "た", "s": 4.25, "e": 4.375, "sm": 4250, "em": 4375, "cs": 29, "ce": 30, "si": 0}, {"i": 13, "w": "時代", "s": 4.388, "e": 4.737, "sm": 4387, "em": 4737, "cs": 30, "ce": 32, "si": 0}, {"i": 14, "w": "に", "s": 